<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13186" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-planto</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To take off a twig</i> or <i>shoot</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Prop.,
				<i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 40, 4</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virgulas de cytiso,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 1, 43</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to break off</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ramum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					2, 2, 26</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> =
			demitto, <i>to set in the ground, to plant</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 17,
				16, 26, § 121</span></i>; <i><span class="en">17, 20, 33, §
			146</span></i>; cf. Voss. ad <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 2, 65</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
